3. Change OSPWebClientService

Inject the same RetryConfig:

private final RetryConfig retryConfig;

Constructor:

@Autowired
public OSPWebClientService(
        @Qualifier("webClientNoAuth") WebClient webClient,
        TokenGenerationWebClientService tokenGenerationWebClientService,
        RetryConfig retryConfig) {

    this.webClient = webClient;
    this.tokenGenerationWebClientService = tokenGenerationWebClientService;
    this.retryConfig = retryConfig;
}

Then replace this entire block:

.retryWhen(Retry.backoff(maxRetryAttempts, Duration.ofSeconds(initialDelay))
        .maxBackoff(...)
        .jitter(...)
        .filter(this::isRetryable)
        .onRetryExhaustedThrow(...))

with:

.retryWhen(
    retryConfig.createRetry(
        maxRetryAttempts,
        initialDelay,
        "OSP API"
    )
)

Then remove:

isRetryable()

from OSPWebClientService.

This means both APIs now use the same centralized retry logging:

TrackingResourceWebClientHelper ──┐
                                  │
OSPWebClientService ──────────────┼──> RetryConfig
                                  │       ↓
                                  │   isRetryable()
                                  │       ↓
                                  │   doBeforeRetry()
                                  │       ↓
                                  │   log attempt
                                  │       ↓
                                  │   retry
                                  │
                                  └──> exhausted → log final exception

That's much cleaner.


